  "output": {
    "svg": "architecture.svg",
    "alt_text": "An authenticated resume request supplies only an opaque checkpoint identifier. Trusted application code loads a server-owned checkpoint, verifies its complete signature and parent chain, rechecks current identity, policy, tool, and exact approval, applies a deterministic migration, and atomically acquires one lease. The effect boundary dispatches one stable operation to the provider. Known receipts or explicitly unknown outcomes produce a signed child checkpoint; unknown outcomes loop through reconciliation without blind redispatch. Current registries, a transactional store, bounded audit evidence, and explicit terminal outcomes support the flow."
